<title>CHINA: Shanghai Cereals &amp; Oils Exchange moves to Pudong.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Cereals &amp; Oils Exchange moves to Pudong.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai Cereals &amp; Oils Exchange (SCOE) will start to trade in its new building in the Pudong New Area on Wednesday, an exchange official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Trading on the exchange was suspended on Tuesday to facilitate the move, the official said.</p>
<p>The SCOE is the first of Shanghai's financial exchanges to move its business to Pudong, the district which the city government hopes will one day become Asia's Wall Street.</p>
<p>The stock exchange, metal exchange and commodity exchange will also move to Pudong in the next couple of years.</p>
</text>
